-- title:
--   Residue degree one above an inert place in M=LK'
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $L$, $K'$, $M$ be number fields with $K$-algebra structures on $L$, $K'$, $M$ and an $L$-algebra and a $K'$-algebra structure on $M$, the towers $K\subseteq L\subseteq M$ and $K\subseteq K'\subseteq M$ being compatible, and let $L/K$ be Galois. Assume $[L:K]=2$, $[K':K]=2$, $[M:K']=[L:K]$, and that every element of $M$ lies in the $K'$-subalgebra generated by the image of $L$ in $M$ (so $M=LK'$). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and suppose every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying under $v$ (i.e. with $w$ contracting to $v$) has ramification index $e(w\mid v)=1$. Let $\mathfrak{v}$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ contracting to $v$ with inertia degree $f(\mathfrak{v}\mid v)=2$, and let $\mathfrak{w}$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_M$ contracting to $\mathfrak{v}$. Then the inertia degree of $\mathfrak{w}$ over $\mathfrak{v}$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the local behaviour at an inert place in the base change of a quadratic Galois extension: if $K'/K$ is inert at $v$ then the places of the compositum $M=LK'$ above such a place of $K'$ have residue degree $1$ over it. It is used in the computation of valuations of norms along $M/K'$ in [`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_valued_eq_exp_inertiaDeg_mul_of_valued_norm_eq_of_baseChange`](thm.html#IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_valued_eq_exp_inertiaDeg_mul_of_valued_norm_eq_of_baseChange).
